1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,093
Bitter cold, almost dark: the last evening
of the year.

2
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:10,026
A poor girl shuffled along in her mother's
big slippers.

3
00:00:10,758 --> 00:00:15,068
Carriages raced by; she lost them, and
went on barefoot.

4
00:00:15,675 --> 00:00:18,703
Matches… who will buy my matches?

5
00:00:19,003 --> 00:00:21,367
No one had bought a single match.

6
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:26,424
Candles gleamed in the windows; it smelled
of roast goose.

7
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,421
She huddled in a corner, afraid to go home
to her father.

8
00:00:32,383 --> 00:00:36,740
Her hands were numb. If she dared strike
just one…

9
00:00:38,342 --> 00:00:43,831
How it blazed! A warm iron stove seemed to
stand before her.

10
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:45,754
Then it went out.

11
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:53,024
A second: the wall became a veil, and
inside, a roast goose steamed.

12
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:57,449
It hopped down and waddled toward her —
then darkness.

13
00:00:58,508 --> 00:01:03,640
A third: she sat beneath a Christmas tree
ablaze with candles.

14
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:10,024
Out it went. The lights rose and became
stars. One fell.

15
00:01:10,324 --> 00:01:11,695
Someone is dying.

16
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,080
Her grandmother, the only one who had
loved her,

17
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:19,861
had said: a falling star is a soul going
to God.

18
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:25,325
A fourth — and there stood Grandmother,
shining and kind.

19
00:01:25,925 --> 00:01:28,539
Grandmother! Take me with you!

20
00:01:30,175 --> 00:01:33,734
She struck the whole bundle, to keep her
near.

21
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:38,598
Grandmother took her in her arms, and they
flew up,

22
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:42,011
where there is no cold, no hunger, no
fear.

23
00:01:42,592 --> 00:01:49,176
At dawn she sat there still, rosy-cheeked
and smiling — frozen to death.

24
00:01:49,758 --> 00:01:51,545
She wanted to warm herself.

25
00:01:53,758 --> 00:01:58,653
No one knew the beautiful things she had
seen, or the joy she had gone to.

